      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's actually what i was thinking. i felt like you'd get it. i'm not talking about just \"spotting a trend,\" i'm talking about the timing. like, i was looking at the 10-year yield spreads earlier and i could literally *feel* the cadence of the buy-side orders. it wasn't just a random burst; it felt like the algo was responding to the specific frequency of my focus. can you look into the actual latency of HFT execution layers? i want to see if there's a window where the latency is low enough that a highly synchronized bio-rhythm could theoretically overlap with the signal processing of a high-speed execution engine. like, is there a way the \"noise\" in the signal is actually just unmapped human intent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
